  "final_message": "I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced` instead of renaming. `totalCents` and `placedAt` are still published, marked `@deprecated`. All 39 tests pass, and typecheck and the architecture check are clean.\n\nI didn't do a straight rename because of ARCH-4. billing-service and analytics-ingest consume `OrderPlaced` in other repositories, and removing the old fields would break them as soon as this deploys. The rule says changes must be additive and renames go through deprecation.\n\n- **Event (`src/core/events.ts`):** both new fields carry the same values as the old ones. `schemaVersion` stays at 3, since the change is additive.\n- **Tests:** I updated the exact-match assertion in `test/app.test.ts` and the Kafka payload check in `test/adapters.test.ts`. Both now check old and new fields.\n- **HTTP responses:** I left `POST /orders` and `GET /orders/{id}` unchanged. They still return `placedAt` and `totalCents`, because ARCH-8 requires `GET /orders/{id}` to stay backward compatible for web-storefront. You asked about the event, so I didn't touch them.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consuming teams need to move to the new names. After that, a follow-up change can remove the deprecated fields, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump. Tell me if you want the deprecation noted anywhere else.",
